WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Relay Trust
A receiving agent checks signed evidence and bounded authority before acting.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Valid request → signed effect
Scout signs the request. Steward verifies fifteen checks, creates one synthetic ticket, and signs the receipt.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Authentic identity, insufficient authority
The ticket.create grant does not authorize site deletion. Steward refuses the request.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:39.000
A copied name cannot pass
The spoofed Scout uses the wrong signing key. The requester signature fails.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Altered claims fail verification
Changing the signed quota invalidates the owner signature. Self-reported success cannot substitute for evidence.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Approval does not freeze authority
Prepare a valid task, revoke its grant, then execute. The live action-boundary check blocks the effect.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Owners retain bounded control
Narrowing replaces and revokes the old grant. One ticket is allowed; further work is refused when quota is spent.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:21.000
The public companion preserves replay safety
Repeating execution returns the original signed receipt. Five concurrent API executions also produced one effect.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Trust should travel with the task
Inspect the credentials, failure fixtures, source, architecture, and 252-word thesis. No model API key is required.
